      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 3.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.45,
      "end_seconds": 9.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.26,
      "end_seconds": 13.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Um, so... headaches. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.66,
      "end_seconds": 16.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.55,
      "end_seconds": 22.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Um, it's been about a month, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.7,
      "end_seconds": 32.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.69,
      "end_seconds": 39.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Uh, I'd say a few times a day. Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.24,
      "end_seconds": 45.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "What about being told it was just stress, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.35,
      "end_seconds": 54.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Yeah, that too. As for being told it was just stress, about a three out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.19,
      "end_seconds": 61.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Any hot flushes, visual changes, weight change or positive pregnancy test at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.87,
      "end_seconds": 68.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "No, no hot flushes, visual changes, weight change or positive pregnancy test."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.63,
      "end_seconds": 75.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.29,
      "end_seconds": 78.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.56,
      "end_seconds": 96.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.68,
      "end_seconds": 100.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.24,
      "end_seconds": 105.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.98,
      "end_seconds": 122.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.25,
      "end_seconds": 127.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "I'm allergic to tramadol, I get feeling very drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.52,
      "end_seconds": 132.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.02,
      "end_seconds": 136.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.99,
      "end_seconds": 142.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.57,
      "end_seconds": 148.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.97,
      "end_seconds": 154.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.66,
      "end_seconds": 164.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.18,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. My partner and our baby. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.62,
      "end_seconds": 180.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.58,
      "end_seconds": 192.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.02,
      "end_seconds": 217.87,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 97 percent, respiratory rate 18, temp 36.6 degrees, pressure 126 over 76, pulse is 73 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.22,
      "end_seconds": 220.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.81,
      "end_seconds": 225.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.01,
      "end_seconds": 231.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.67,
      "end_seconds": 234.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Right, does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.88,
      "end_seconds": 251.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "You are not pregnant by the urine test, the breasts express a little milk, and there is no visual field loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.47,
      "end_seconds": 258.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.79,
      "end_seconds": 294.22,
      "duration_seconds": 25.43,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. It points towards raised prolactin or a thyroid problem rather than stress. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. A prolactin and thyroid blood test is what I'd like next, for galactorrhoea. Don't stress about stress as the cause, the tests will tell us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.57,
      "end_seconds": 308.94,
      "duration_seconds": 14.37,
      "text": "I follow. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. I'd like to see you again after the results. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.31,
      "end_seconds": 314.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Mm, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}